<!-- Exegesis English Exposition -->
<div class="commentary-text font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface flex flex-col gap-space-sm leading-relaxed">
<p>
            Imām Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Kathīr (رحمه الله) records that this sublime verse contains ten independent theological assertions confirming the unicity, self-subsistence, and absolute sovereignty of Allāh.
          </p>
<p>
            Regarding <strong class="text-primary font-semibold">«ٱلۡحَىُّ ٱلۡقَيُّومُ» (Al-Ḥayyu al-Qayyūm)</strong>: He is the Ever-Living Who never dies, possessing primordial vitality without inception or terminus. <em>Al-Qayyūm</em> designates the Self-Sustaining Master through Whose sovereign will all creation is upheld and sustained without fatigue.
          </p>
<!-- Authentic Hadith Reference Card -->
<div class="p-space-md rounded-xl bg-surface-container shadow-sm flex flex-col gap-1">
